= Appendix H — Eight-Week Study Plan

+ *Week 1:* Foundations; read chapter 1, attempt its drill and record reasons for errors.
+ *Week 2:* Skeleton and joints; label a diagram and practise movement terms.
+ *Week 3:* Muscles and nerves; explain muscle pairs and reflex pathways.
+ *Week 4:* Circulation and respiration; trace blood flow and practise pulse calculations.
+ *Week 5:* Fitness; apply FITT and training principles to realistic examples.
+ *Week 6:* Athletics; revise events, measurement and safe organisation.
+ *Week 7:* Games and competition; compare skills, fixtures and fair play.
+ *Week 8:* Recreation and inclusion; attempt both timed papers on separate occasions.

After each week, mark the drill and read every explanation. Revisit uncertain items after a gap. Use the master bank for another check and update the plan to address weak areas. Schedule rest and adapt physical activities to individual circumstances.
